  "label": "monkey is mapped to monkey blood",
  "description": "The text 'monkey blood' is overlaid on the image of a dead monkey with visible blood, creating an analogical mapping where the visual entity (the dead monkey with blood) is explicitly identified or labeled by the textual entity ('monkey blood'). This mapping reinforces the racist trope by equating the visual representation of a dead monkey with the textual label, thereby projecting the concept of 'monkey blood' directly onto the visual material. The mapping is direct and explicit, using the text to categorize or define the visual content.",
